---
import Landing from '../../layouts/Landing.astro';
import FeatureSection from '../../components/FeatureSection.astro';
import CtaBanner from '../../components/CtaBanner.astro';
---

<Landing
  title="Bilbycast — Every capability"
  description="Every Bilbycast capability on one page. Twelve protocols, in-process transcoding, audio gateway, FEC, hitless redundancy, NMOS, AI-assisted configuration, and more."
>
  <section class="pt-32 pb-8 lg:pt-40 lg:pb-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">Every capability, on one page</h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
        The full Bilbycast transport, processing and control feature list, no curation. If you're evaluating against a
        procurement checklist or a competitive matrix, this is the page to bookmark. Several shipped capabilities are
        documented on their own pages rather than carded below —
        <a href="/edge/replay/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Replay</a> (continuous recording plus clip
        playback, on in every release binary),
        <a href="/edge/display/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">local display output</a> (HDMI / DisplayPort
        plus ALSA confidence monitoring, also default-on), and the relay's
        <a href="/relay/viewer-distribution/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">viewer distribution</a> — a WHEP
        SFU and an LL-HLS origin with a browser DVR player. Read top-to-bottom or jump to the headlines on the
        <a href="/features/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">four pillars</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FeatureSection />

  <CtaBanner />
</Landing>
